# Version pins for incus-compose-update. Image refs in compose.yaml
# interpolate these; check/apply reads and writes them. Tracked in git.
# Secrets stay in .env (gitignored).
#
# Every pin here is a DIGEST, with the human-readable tag left literal in
# compose.yaml (`image:label@${DIGEST}`) — the same shape Search_Providers
# uses for nuq-postgres. Tags are mutable and, as the relay incident below
# shows, tag *ordering* can be actively wrong; a digest cannot be.
#
# Pin targets verified 2026-08-26.

# Buzz relay — digest of the `main` tag.
#
# Why not a version tag: none exist. `v0.5.2`, `0.5.2` and `v0.4.26` all 404
# in the registry; every GitHub release since 2026-07-31 is `desktop-v0.5.x`
# (the Tauri app), which publishes no relay image. `:latest` is stale (built
# 2026-08-08, mislabelled version 0.2.1) and is NOT an alias for `:main`.
#
# Why not `sha-<7>` ranked by push time: TRIED, AND IT BROKE THE STACK.
# `order: pushed` chose sha-001151e — built 2026-07-16, six weeks older than
# the sha-822c5ab it replaced. Push timestamps in this registry do not track
# build time. The relay refused to start (`migration 20 was previously
# applied but is missing in the resolved migrations`) and had to be rolled
# back. `:main` is rebuilt from HEAD, so its digest is always current.
#
# This digest == commit sha-4f529a4, built 2026-08-26T10:33Z. To recover the
# commit from any digest, read org.opencontainers.image.revision — the
# README has the one-liner.
BUZZ_DIGEST=sha256:d689c07db473b38f395871b8a320a88e5f2d45e79866b750ba1092edb4cc4f4d

# Postgres — digest of 18-alpine. The MAJOR VERSION IS LITERAL in
# compose.yaml and must stay that way: PG18 binaries refuse to start against
# a PG17 data directory, so a major bump is a pg_upgrade/dump-restore
# project, not a pin change. Keeping the major out of this file means
# `apply-all` can never perform one by accident.
POSTGRES_DIGEST=sha256:77f585114c32fbca283dc835b0596f4e52b51b4c6662d7810b2f4084f60a1873

# Redis — digest of 7-alpine, currently 7.4.11.
REDIS_DIGEST=sha256:858f009f9709ce576febc734aa78b8f6d624b82571f9ddb6bda4377c833b3499

# MinIO and its client. Literal immutable RELEASE tags copied from upstream's
# bundle: these are the versions Buzz is tested against, so they move when
# upstream moves, not when the registry does. No x-update block for either.
MINIO_TAG=RELEASE.2025-09-07T16-13-09Z
MINIO_MC_TAG=RELEASE.2025-08-13T08-35-41Z
